      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was actually trying to point out the equivalent of the old behaviour where TryCancelUpdate() would return false triggering below condition which is before `needs_merge` check.\n\n```\nif (!TryCancelUpdate(\u0026needs_merge)) {\n        return false;\n}\n```\n\nPreviously TryCancelUpdate would return `false` for\n1. LockExclusive() fails \u003d\u003d\u003e CancelResult::ERROR\n2. IsSnapshotWithoutSlotSwitch() \u003d\u003d\u003e CancelResult::LIVE_SNAPSHOTS\n3. RemoveAllUpdateState() fails \u003d\u003d\u003e Ignored in new implementation\n\nFor all these 3 conditions, we would not continue BeginUpdate() and would return false. New implementation ignores all these 3 cases, it wasn\u0027t clear to me if this was intentional. If not, check for this should be before `(TryCancelUpdate() \u003d\u003d CancelResult::NEEDS_MERGE)` check.",
